mbaexchange-ebury:greenhouse:4876058101.descriptionHtml:
&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;Ebury helps ambitious businesses unlock global growth, and we take the same approach with our people. We encourage innovation and movement, collaboration and problem-solving, and foster an environment where everyone can feel they belong, are valued, supported and empowered to succeed.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;If you’re a collaborator who wants to help transform how businesses operate globally, get in touch - we’d love to discuss how Ebury can accelerate your career so you can shape the future.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;text-decoration: underline;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Senior Product Manager&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;strong&gt; - FX Expansion&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Ebury London Office - Hybrid: 4 days in the office, 1 day working from home per week&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As the Senior Product Manager for FX Expansion, you will move beyond the day-to-day &quot;build&quot; and focus entirely on growth and scale. Your mission is to identify where our next FX Product growth will come from by aggressively expanding our FX product suite and launching into new products and geographic territories.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This is not a &quot;maintenance&quot; role. You will not be bogged down by technical debt or backlog grooming; instead, you will act as a financial product architect and Global Subject Matter Expert (SME), determining how our existing FX capabilities can be adapted, enhanced, and deployed to drive our FX product expansion.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you’ll do&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;div id=&quot;page-1&quot; class=&quot;_kqswh2mm _bfhku67f _18u01wug _2hwx1wug&quot; data-testid=&quot;page-0&quot;&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Geographic Expansion &amp;amp; Market Entry&lt;/strong&gt;: Lead the product roadmap for entering new countries. You will define the tasks and developments required for success in specific regions (e.g., LATAM, APAC), ensuring our FX products comply with local market nuances while maintaining global scalability.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Product Suite Diversification&lt;/strong&gt;: Identify gaps in our current FX offering. You will spearhead the launch of new product variations and capabilities—such as exotic currency pairs, product processes, or structured derivatives—to meet the needs of diverse global enterprises.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Cross-Domain Program Managemen&lt;/strong&gt;t: Lead high-impact, crossfunctional programs that span multiple domains. You will be responsible for orchestrating project delivery across Legal, Compliance, Treasury, and Sales to ensure that expansion initiatives are integrated seamlessly across the entire organization.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Knowledge Governance &amp;amp; Documentation&lt;/strong&gt;: Own the end-to-end &quot;Source of Truth&quot; for the FX product suite. You will ensure that all product documentation—including internal playbooks, API technical specifications, and client-facing guides—is of the highest quality, technically accurate, and continuously updated.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Global FX SME&lt;/strong&gt;: Serve as the definitive Subject Matter Expert for the FX domain. You will provide strategic guidance to other product areas and senior leadership, ensuring Ebury’s FX logic and market mechanics are understood and correctly implemented across all global channels.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Commercial Growth Strategy&lt;/strong&gt;: Shift the focus from &quot;features&quot; to &quot;revenue.&quot; You will work closely with Sales and Trading to understand and build the FX product strategy to drive client growth.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;High-Level Stakeholder Influence&lt;/strong&gt;: Act as the bridge between regional heads and global leadership. You will provide the business case for expansion, justifying investment based on market size, regulatory ease, and competitive advantage.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you’ll need&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;5+ years in Product Management: Specifically within FX or Global Payments, with a proven track record of launching products in multiple jurisdictions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;FX Domain Mastery: Deep derivative knowledge (Spot, Forwards, NDFs, and Options) and the regulatory frameworks (e.g., MiFID II) that govern them globally.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Project &amp;amp; Program Management: Demonstrated experience managing complex, multi-departmental projects with a focus on timeline adherence and dependency management.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;User-Centric Approach: A relentless focus on solving user friction points; you use research and data to ensure expansion efforts deliver immediate value.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Market Entry Specialist: You have successfully taken a financial product from &quot;concept&quot; to &quot;live&quot; in different global regions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Growth Mindset: You are bored by &quot;business as usual.&quot; You are driven by KPIs related to volume growth, client acquisition, and geographic footprint.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Communication Excellence: Ability to influence C-suite stakeholders and lead cross-functional teams without direct authority.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Why Ebury?&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Competitive Starting Salary&lt;/strong&gt; with an &lt;strong&gt;annual discretionary bonus&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;that truly rewards your performance from day one.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Dedicated Mentorship: &lt;/strong&gt;Learn directly from experienced managers who are invested in your success.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Cutting-Edge Technology: &lt;/strong&gt;Leverage state-of-the-art tailor made tools and systems that enable you to perform at your best.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Clear, Accelerated Career Progression: &lt;/strong&gt;Defined pathways to leadership and specialist roles within Ebury.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Dynamic &amp;amp; Supportive Culture: &lt;/strong&gt;Work in a collaborative environment where teamwork and personal growth are prioritized.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Generous Benefits Package: &lt;/strong&gt;Access competitive benefits tailored to your location, which typically include health care and social benefits.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Central London&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Office: A fantastic location with excellent transport links.&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Ready to launch your career with a global FinTech? Click the ‘Apply’ Today and discover your potential at Ebury!&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You can also connect with me on LinkedIn&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;#LI-FZ1&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About us&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Ebury delivers sophisticated, integrated solutions — business accounts, hedging, and financing — on a single platform with a seamless workflow. Our success is built on a simple premise and singular purpose: To help businesses operate and scale globally.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Since its founding in 2009, Ebury has always been a fast-growing leader in fintech. Today, we bring together 1,800+ Eburians across nearly 70 cities and we’re always looking to add to our team.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;At the heart of our offering is a proprietary platform, purpose-built to help businesses seamlessly streamline and manage global cash flow. We focus on continuous product evolution and innovation to build the infrastructure for borderless growth and help our clients scale at every stage.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The opportunities at Ebury are as diverse as our people, ranging from business development to engineering roles across our tech pillars.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We believe in inclusion. We stand against discrimination in all forms and are against the intolerance of differences that makes us a modern and successful organisation. At Ebury, you can be whoever you want to be and still feel a sense of belonging no matter your story.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;

mbaexchange-guidepoint:greenhouse:819089.descriptionHtml:
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Overview:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Guidepoint&#39;s Engineering team thrives on delivering innovative technology solutions that accelerate revenue growth, reduce costs and increase efficiency and productivity. As Guidepoint works to achieve it&#39;s mission of making individuals, businesses, and the world smarter through personalized knowledge-sharing solutions, the engineering team is taking on challenges to create new products, improve existing platforms to optimize the seamless delivery of our services.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;This is a hybrid position based in Toronto.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What You&#39;ll Do:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Design, build, and maintain scalable test automation frameworks.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Automate functional, API, and integration test cases by developing reusable and maintainable automated scripts.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Analyze and troubleshoot issues related to automated and load testing, propose solutions, and enhance existing scripts where needed.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Review test results, determine root causes of failures, assess severity and scope, and guide prioritization for resolution.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collaborate with developers to integrate automated tests into CI/CD pipelines, ensuring quality at every stage of delivery.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Provide regular updates on defects, regression test status, and automation progress through Jira and other reporting tools.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Assist in planning, developing, and delivering training on test automation frameworks and tools.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Maintain clear documentation of automation processes, templates, and best practices while driving process improvements.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner closely with engineering teams, product owners, and QA peers in Agile environments to define acceptance criteria and testing approaches.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Stay updated with technology trends and continuously improve test automation practices.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support functional and regression testing efforts as needed to ensure end-to-end quality.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What You Have:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;3–6 years of experience in an SDET or QA Automation engineering role with significant hands-on API automation experience.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong programming skills in Java for test automation.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proven experience with automated testing tools and practices (e.g., Selenium or similar) along with Web Service / API testing.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Hands-on experience testing REST APIs using tools or frameworks such as RestAssured, Postman (automation), or similar.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Solid understanding of HTTP protocols, API contracts, and service-oriented architectures (SOA).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Solid understanding of the software development lifecycle (SDLC) and exposure to Agile, Waterfall, and Scrum.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with performance/load testing tools and approaches, including APIs.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity with ticketing systems (Jira preferred).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;In-depth knowledge of SOA frameworks, processes, strategies, and approaches.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Practical experience with CI/CD and DevOps tools, with the ability to integrate API and UI automation into delivery pipelines.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Bachelor’s degree in Computer Science, Computer Engineering, Information Technology, or related field.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What We Offer:&lt;/strong&gt; &amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The annual base salary range for this position is $100,000 - $130,000. Additionally, this position is eligible for an annual discretionary bonus based on performance.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;You will also be eligible for the following benefits:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Paid Time Off&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Comprehensive benefits plan&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Company RRSP Match&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Development opportunities through the LinkedIn Learning platform&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About Guidepoint:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Guidepoint is a leading research enablement platform designed to advance understanding and empower our clients’ decision-making process. Powered by innovative technology, real-time data, and hard-to-source expertise, we help our clients to turn answers into action.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Backed by a network of nearly 1.75 million experts and Guidepoint’s 1,600 employees worldwide, we inform leading organizations’ research by delivering on-demand intelligence and research on request. With Guidepoint, companies and investors can better navigate the abundance of information available today, making it both more useful and more powerful.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;At Guidepoint, our success relies on the diversity of our employees, advisors, and client base, which allows us to create connections that offer a wealth of perspectives. We are committed to upholding policies that contribute to&amp;nbsp;an equitable&amp;nbsp;and welcoming environment for our community, regardless of background, identity, or experience.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
